  ('calc-integration/ftc-part-2', 'calc-integration', 12, 'FTC Part 2 (net change): $\int_a^b F''(x)\,dx = \,?$', '$F(b) - F(a)$

The definite integral of a rate of change is the **net change** in the original quantity. Here $F$ is any antiderivative of $f = F''$.

Example: $\int_0^1 x^2\,dx = F(1) - F(0)$ with $F(x) = \frac{x^3}{3}$, so the value is $\frac13$.
