  ('calc-integration/ftc-part-1-chain-rule', 'calc-integration', 13, '$\frac{d}{dx}\int_1^{x^2} \cos t\,dt = \,?$', '$2x\cos(x^2)$

FTC Part 1 says $\frac{d}{dx}\int_a^x f(t)\,dt = f(x)$. With upper limit $g(x)$ the chain rule adds a factor: $f(g(x))\,g''(x)$.

A constant lower limit does not matter.

