  ('calc-integration/ftc-sine-zero-to-pi', 'calc-integration', 17, 'Evaluate $\int_0^{\pi} \sin x\,dx$.', '$2$

An antiderivative is $-\cos x$, so the value is $-\cos\pi - (-\cos 0) = 1 + 1 = 2$.

