  ('calc-integration/area-function-local-max', 'calc-integration', 20, 'Let $g(x) = \int_0^x f(t)\,dt$ with $f$ continuous. Where does $g$ have a local maximum?', 'Where $f$ changes sign from positive to negative

By FTC Part 1, $g''(x) = f(x)$. So the critical points of $g$ are the zeros of $f$, and the first derivative test applies to $f$''s sign changes.

