  ('calc-integration/u-sub-different-forms', 'calc-integration', 41, '$\int \sin x\cos x\,dx$: $u = \sin x$ gives $\frac12\sin^2 x + C$, but $u = \cos x$ gives $-\frac12\cos^2 x + C$. Which is right?', 'Both

