Tip: $\sin\frac{\pi}{4}$ and $\cos\frac{\pi}{4}$ are equal.', 'sqrt(2)/2', array['sqrt2/2', '1/sqrt(2)', '1/sqrt2', '(sqrt(2))/2', '(sqrt2)/2']::text[], '$\dfrac{\sqrt{2}}{2}$', 'sin pi/4 exact value sqrt2/2'),
  ('trig-unit-circle/cos-pi-over-6', 'trig-unit-circle', 56, 'Exact value of $\cos\frac{\pi}{6}$?', '$\dfrac{\sqrt{3}}{2}$

The $30^\circ$ point is $\left(\frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}, \frac{1}{2}\right)$, and cosine is the $x$-coordinate.

Tip: a small angle''s point sits far to the right, so its cosine is the larger coordinate.
Watch out: do not swap with $\sin\frac{\pi}{6} = \frac{1}{2}$.', 'sqrt(3)/2', array['sqrt3/2', '(sqrt(3))/2', '(sqrt3)/2']::text[], '$\dfrac{\sqrt{3}}{2}$', 'cos pi/6 exact value sqrt3/2'),
  ('trig-unit-circle/tan-45-degrees', 'trig-unit-circle', 57, 'Exact value of $\tan 45^\circ$?', '$1$

At $45^\circ$ the two coordinates are equal, so $\tan 45^\circ = \frac{\sqrt{2}/2}{\sqrt{2}/2} = 1$.

Tip: tangent is $\pm 1$ at every odd multiple of $45^\circ$.', '1', '{}'::text[], '$1$', 'tan 45 degrees exact value 1'),
  ('trig-unit-circle/sin-3pi-over-2', 'trig-unit-circle', 58, 'Exact value of $\sin\frac{3\pi}{2}$?', '$-1$

