Its cosine is $0$, so $\tan\frac{3\pi}{2}$ is undefined.
Tip: the four axis points are $(1,0)$, $(0,1)$, $(-1,0)$, $(0,-1)$ at $0$, $\frac{\pi}{2}$, $\pi$, $\frac{3\pi}{2}$.', '-1', '{}'::text[], '$-1$', 'sin 3pi/2 value unit circle'),
  ('trig-unit-circle/cot-pi-over-2', 'trig-unit-circle', 59, 'Exact value of $\cot\frac{\pi}{2}$?', '$0$

$\cot\frac{\pi}{2} = \frac{\cos(\pi/2)}{\sin(\pi/2)} = \frac{0}{1} = 0$.

Watch out: $\tan\frac{\pi}{2}$ is undefined, but cotangent at the same angle is simply $0$.', '0', '{}'::text[], '$0$', 'cot pi/2 value cotangent'),
  ('trig-unit-circle/sec-pi', 'trig-unit-circle', 60, 'Exact value of $\sec\pi$?', '$-1$

$\pi$ lands at $(-1, 0)$, so $\cos\pi = -1$ and $\sec\pi = \frac{1}{-1} = -1$.

Tip: secant equals $\pm 1$ exactly where cosine does, at the multiples of $\pi$.', '-1', '{}'::text[], '$-1$', 'sec pi value secant'),
  ('trig-unit-circle/cos-3pi-over-4', 'trig-unit-circle', 61, 'Exact value of $\cos\frac{3\pi}{4}$?', '$-\dfrac{\sqrt{2}}{2}$

$\frac{3\pi}{4} = \pi - \frac{\pi}{4}$ is in QII with **reference angle** $\frac{\pi}{4}$, and cosine is negative in QII.

So $\cos\frac{3\pi}{4} = -\cos\frac{\pi}{4} = -\frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}$.
Watch out: $\cos\frac{3\pi}{4}$ is not $+\frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}$; the $x$-coordinate is left of the $y$-axis.', '-sqrt(2)/2', array['-sqrt2/2', '-1/sqrt(2)', '-1/sqrt2', '-(sqrt(2)/2)', '-(sqrt2)/2']::text[], '$-\dfrac{\sqrt{2}}{2}$', 'cos 3pi/4 exact value'),
  ('trig-unit-circle/sin-5pi-over-6', 'trig-unit-circle', 62, 'Exact value of $\sin\frac{5\pi}{6}$?', '$\dfrac{1}{2}$

