  ('diffeq-first-order/bernoulli-trivial-cases', 'diffeq-first-order', 53, 'Why is a Bernoulli equation linear already when $n = 0$ or $n = 1$?', 'For $n = 0$ it is $y'' + py = q$. For $n = 1$ it is $y'' + (p - q)y = 0$.

