  ('diffeq-first-order/existence-uniqueness-theorem', 'diffeq-first-order', 58, 'Existence and uniqueness theorem for $y'' = f(x,y)$, $y(x_0) = y_0$?', 'If $f$ and $\dfrac{\partial f}{\partial y}$ are continuous near $(x_0, y_0)$, there is a **unique** solution on some interval around $x_0$.

