  ('diffeq-first-order/autonomous-monotone', 'diffeq-first-order', 77, 'Why is every solution of an autonomous $y'' = f(y)$ monotone?', 'Solutions cannot cross equilibria (uniqueness), so $f$ keeps one sign along a solution.

