  ('sw-data-structures/singly-linked-delete-tail', 'sw-data-structures', 38, 'A singly linked list keeps both head and tail pointers. Why is removing the last node still $O(n)$?', 'The new tail is the second-to-last node, and with no `prev` pointers the only way to reach it is to walk from the head.

