  ('sw-data-structures/sentinel-node', 'sw-data-structures', 39, 'What is a sentinel (dummy) node in a linked list, and why use one?', 'A permanent placeholder node at the head (and often the tail) that holds no real data.

Why: every real node then has a predecessor (and, with a tail sentinel, a successor), so insert and delete need no special cases for an empty list or for the first and last nodes.', null, '{}'::text[], null, 'linked list sentinel dummy node purpose'),
  ('sw-data-structures/reverse-linked-list-space', 'sw-data-structures', 40, 'Extra space needed to reverse a singly linked list of $n$ nodes iteratively?', '$O(1)$ extra space, in $O(n)$ time.

Walk the list once, flipping each `next` pointer:

