Key idea: equal objects must have equal hash codes, so override `hashCode` whenever you override `equals`.', null, '{}'::text[], null, 'Java equals hashCode contract HashMap broken'),
  ('sw-data-structures/division-method-power-of-two', 'sw-data-structures', 55, 'With the division-method hash $h(k) = k \bmod m$, why is a power of two such as $m = 2^{10}$ a poor table size?', '$k \bmod 2^p$ is just the lowest $p$ bits of $k$, so keys that differ only in their higher bits all collide.

