  ('sw-data-structures/inorder-sorted', 'sw-data-structures', 62, 'Which depth-first traversal of a binary search tree visits its keys in sorted order?', 'In-order: left subtree, then the node, then the right subtree.

It lists all $n$ keys in $O(n)$ time, so a BST yields a **sorted** sequence without a separate sort.

Tip: pre-order visits the node first; post-order visits it last.', 'in-order', array['inorder', 'in-order traversal', 'inorder traversal']::text[], null, 'BST in-order traversal sorted order'),
  ('sw-data-structures/preorder-worked', 'sw-data-structures', 63, 'Insert $5, 3, 8, 1, 4$ into an empty BST, in that order. What is the tree''s pre-order traversal?', '$5, 3, 1, 4, 8$

The tree has $5$ at the root with children $3$ and $8$, and $1$ and $4$ under $3$. Pre-order visits the node, then its left subtree, then its right subtree.

Watch out: in-order would give $1, 3, 4, 5, 8$ instead.', '5 3 1 4 8', array['5, 3, 1, 4, 8', '[5, 3, 1, 4, 8]']::text[], '$5, 3, 1, 4, 8$', 'BST insert 5 3 8 1 4 pre-order traversal'),
  ('sw-data-structures/level-order-queue', 'sw-data-structures', 64, 'Level-order (breadth-first) traversal of a binary tree keeps the nodes waiting to be visited in which data structure?', 'A queue (FIFO).

