  ('sw-data-structures/tree-rotation', 'sw-data-structures', 67, 'What does a single rotation in a BST preserve, and what does it cost?', 'It preserves the in-order sequence of keys, so the BST property still holds, while moving one node up and another down to change subtree heights.

A rotation rewires a constant number of pointers, so it''s $O(1)$.

Key idea: AVL and red-black trees rebalance with rotations.', null, '{}'::text[], null, 'BST rotation preserves in-order cost O(1)'),
  ('sw-data-structures/avl-lr-case', 'sw-data-structures', 68, 'AVL insertion: node $z$ becomes left-heavy, and its left child $y$ is right-heavy (the left-right case). Which rotations fix it?', 'A double rotation: first rotate left at $y$, then rotate right at $z$.

