  ('chem-thermo-kinetics/pseudo-first-order-conditions', 'chem-thermo-kinetics', 73, 'What is a pseudo-first-order reaction, and how is it created?', 'A reaction whose rate depends on **one** concentration because the other reactant is in large excess.

If $[\ce{B}]$ is huge, it stays essentially constant, so rate $= k[\ce{A}][\ce{B}] \approx k''[\ce{A}]$ with $k'' = k[\ce{B}]$.

