  ('stats-distributions/exponential-survival-function', 'stats-distributions', 51, 'For an exponential waiting time with rate $\lambda$, what is $P(X > t)$?', '$P(X > t) = e^{-\lambda t}$ for $t \ge 0$

The density is $f(x) = \lambda e^{-\lambda x}$ and the CDF is $F(t) = 1 - e^{-\lambda t}$.

