  ('stats-distributions/exponential-rate-to-mean', 'stats-distributions', 52, 'Customers arrive at a rate of $\lambda = 4$ per hour, with exponential times between arrivals. What is the mean time between arrivals, in minutes?', '$15\,\mathrm{min}$

The exponential mean is $\frac{1}{\lambda} = \frac{1}{4}$ hour $= 15\,\mathrm{min}$.

