  ('stats-distributions/exponential-exceed-mean', 'stats-distributions', 53, 'Bulb lifetimes are exponential with mean $1000\,\mathrm{h}$. What fraction of bulbs last longer than the mean? Round to 3 decimal places.', '$e^{-1} \approx 0.368$

$P(X > 1000) = e^{-1000/1000} = e^{-1} \approx 0.368$

