  ('stats-distributions/se-vs-sd', 'stats-distributions', 79, 'What is the difference between a standard deviation and a standard error?', 'The SD measures how much **individual observations** vary; the standard error measures how much a **statistic**, such as $\bar{x}$, varies from sample to sample.

