  ('stats-distributions/finite-population-correction', 'stats-distributions', 81, 'Sampling $n$ items without replacement from a population of $N$, what factor corrects the standard error of $\bar{x}$?', '$\sqrt{\dfrac{N-n}{N-1}}$, the finite population correction: $\mathrm{SE} = \dfrac{\sigma}{\sqrt{n}}\sqrt{\dfrac{N-n}{N-1}}$

